UPSTREAM SOURCES

  DataSF, data.sfgov.org, City and County of San Francisco. DataSF's Terms of Use (section IX) say: "Data is made
  available under the Public Domain Dedication and License v1.0, unless a file or page says otherwise." Each dataset
  below states the Open Data Commons Public Domain Dedication and License (PDDL),
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/pddl/1.0/
    - Soft-Story Properties (Mandatory Soft Story Program), dataset beah-shgi, data as of 7 October 2026.
      https://data.sfgov.org/d/beah-shgi
    - Building Permits, dataset i98e-djp9: the permits whose description names the soft story retrofit work.
      https://data.sfgov.org/d/i98e-djp9
    - Parcels - Active and Retired, dataset acdm-wktn: the outlines of the listed parcels.
      https://data.sfgov.org/d/acdm-wktn
    Changes: one row per parcel (a parcel listed under two addresses keeps the least finished status); each parcel's
    completion date is the earliest completed date of a completed soft story permit on it; parcels joined to their
    outlines by block and lot.

  California Department of Conservation, California Geological Survey: CGS Seismic Hazards Program, Liquefaction
  Zones (Seismic Hazard Zones). Listed on data.ca.gov under Creative Commons Attribution,
  https://data.ca.gov/dataset/cgs-liquefaction-zones
  Changes: the zones in San Francisco merged into one area and split into its separate pieces (43 over 0.2 ha); a
  parcel counts as in a zone when a point inside it is.

